# Aura 2.1.0 — Kodi 21 Omega alpha preparation

A continuation by kcook98765 of **Aura by jurialmunkey**:
https://github.com/jurialmunkey/skin.aura
Source: https://github.com/kcook98765/skin.aura

**Alpha candidate, not yet published or natively accepted.** This build targets
Kodi 21 Omega only (GUI API 5.17.0). Existing Omega development, layout, main
interface typography and add-on ID `skin.aura` are retained. Kodi 19/20 historical
branches and tags remain in Git; they are not this distribution's supported lanes.
Kodi 22 is unqualified. A minimum GUI dependency is not an upper-version bound;
the repository catalog supplies Omega-only routing.

## Proposed repository installation

After separately approved publication, use the existing kcook-lab-repo source:
https://kcook98765.github.io/kcook-lab-repo/
Kodi File manager → Add source; then Add-ons → Install from zip file and select
repository.ai.kodi-0.1.1.zip. Choose Install from repository → kcook-lab-repo →
Look and feel → Skin → Aura. Aura's `xbmc.gui.skin` extension supplies the native
skin category; no custom launcher or new repository installer is needed.
This candidate is not yet available there. Let Kodi install dependencies from
the official Kodi Add-on repository; an index audit is not installation proof.

**Identity conflict:** Kodi identifies this skin as `skin.aura`, the same ID as
other Aura forks. Installing it can replace/update an existing Aura and reuse its
settings. A higher version from another enabled repository may win an update.
Check origin, installed version and per-add-on update settings before installing;
back up the stopped profile. No side-by-side installation or automatic migration
is promised. Do not change an existing working profile just to try this alpha.

## Alpha changes and limits

Five restricted/unclear lyric fonts use licensed bundled alternatives. Language
flags become language-code labels. Photographic album fallbacks become simple
original geometric artwork. Optional unverified photo/view previews and inherited
screenshots are omitted; title art now identifies Omega alpha. Title/fallback art
is not a screenshot. Main appearance and functional Omega work remain retained.

Populated-library widgets, playback/PVR backend behavior, enrichment, animated
lyrics, Backup/Restore and migration acceptance remain incomplete. Online metadata
enrichment is off by default. Dependencies may still use the network. Existing
widgets using removed Skin Helper providers need manual source reselection;
saved shortcuts are not automatically translated. Do not reset a profile to
force migration. The airing calendar is not identical to the old Next Aired guide.

## Owner-reported production experience

The owner reports using their customized Omega 2.1.0 development candidate on
an existing production Kodi Omega instance for more than one week, stable in
normal daily use. Minor layout adjustments remain. This is genuine owner-reported
general use, not formal scripted or scenario-by-scenario acceptance. The installed
file inventory and exact Kodi patch/platform have not been verified against this
cleaned distribution package. The excluded/replaced assets therefore have no new
native acceptance claim. Release preparation performs no new native test.

## Testing and recovery

For any future separately requested testing, use a disposable profile and
synthetic local media. This release campaign performs no installation, skin
switch, profile reset or new native test. Keep Estuary installed. Roll back through Settings →
Interface → Skin → Estuary; switching skins does not restore settings or data.
Native installation and skin switching have not been performed for this candidate.
The Backup add-on needs a configured destination, Add-on Data and custom assets,
and a verified restore. Installing Backup alone creates no backup. Old Skin Helper
backup archives are unsupported. Keep profiles, backups and settings out of Git.

Source guides: docs/TESTING.md, docs/PACKAGING.md, docs/PUBLICATION.md and
docs/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSE-REVIEW.md. These development files are intentionally
excluded from the installable ZIP; the root notices and all font licenses ship.

